  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPM-022",
   "what_failed": "Per-player suppression ranking across many sequential play-type cells.",
   "why": "Recorded as inconclusive (E_unclear): rank-1 deltas mostly within 1-2 SE, no multiple-comparison control, and an OTHER artifact flagged in the document."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-050",
   "what_failed": "Per-star sequential suppression cells with very small post-event samples.",
   "why": "Recorded as E_unclear with no multiplicity correction. Several PUTBACK cells have n_after of 32-95, and the record flags the risk of drift and non-stationarity."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "Play-type labels derived from the current initiation_type mapping are not usable as-is: the recorded audit maps only 0.7% of possessions to a real play type and finds foul-ending contamination in OTHER, DRIVE and PNR.",
  "Foul endings are a recorded confound for play-type PPP comparisons, so any PNR PPP contrast must handle them explicitly.",
  "Sequential-pair analyses in this project have produced positive aftershock and pair-premium results (FAM:SF07), but these do not address the DRIVE->PNR contrast specifically.",
  "Small post-event cells and missing multiplicity control have already produced unreliable per-player sequential results (FAM:SF-APPM-022, FAM:SF-APPA-050)."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "Any estimate of the effect of a teammate DRIVE preceding a PNR on PNR PPP. No retrieved record tests this sequence.",
  "Whether a teammate DRIVE raises PNR PPP beyond the general sequential-pair premium in FAM:SF07.",
  "Whether the labeling defect has been repaired in the current graph database or in the 2025-26 partial data.",
  "Whether the sequential-pair results (FAM:SF07) survive foul-ending adjustment, since its recorded n and validation status are limited."
 ],
